meta {
  name: Update staff member
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/staff/{{staffId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "designation": "Head of Mathematics",
    "employment_type": "full_time"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.designation: eq Head of Mathematics
  res.body.employment_type: eq full_time
}

docs {
  A promotion, which on this model is a plain field edit: designation is a
  label, not a role. Nothing a person is allowed to do follows from it.
  Permissions come from CAS groups, and class and subject responsibility comes
  from the teacher assignments in folder 06.

  employment_type is an enum and a bad value is a 400, not a silently ignored
  field - unlike the query filters on the list routes, where an unrecognised
  value is dropped. Bodies are strict, filters are lenient.

  Ending employment is leaving_date plus status, not a delete. Deleting a staff
  row loses the history that says who taught what.
}
